    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so if the science is so settled, why do some researchers still argue that genetic clusters exist that map to these groups? like, if you look at certain genomic data, people say you can see these distinct ancestral lines. does that support the idea that these aren't just social constructs, or is there a way to be objective about the biological differences without it being racist?",
