      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While genomic science accurately identifies broad geographical ancestries (like West African vs. East Siberian), these \"clusters\" exist primarily along continental lines rather than within them, meaning there is far more genetic diversity within any racial group than between them. Objective biological data confirms that human genetic variation is too continuous and clinal to allow for meaningful division into distinct races, so linking these tiny continental differences to hotspots for complex traits like intelligence is statistically unsound. Furthermore, studies attempting to find genetic markers for race show that the very small amount of genetic difference between \"races\" is drowned out by massive environmental and lifestyle influences, rendering any claims of innate cognitive disparity biologically implausible.",
